{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "transport_flux_n",
    "description": "Scalar atom of the B-grid north-edge advective mass flux of the conservative transport: F_n = HTN * ((vW + vE)/2) * ((cS + cN)/2), the centered corner-average reconstruction of the CICE transport edge algebra. The north edge of T cell (i,j) runs between the two corner U points U(i-1,j) (west endpoint, velocity vW) and U(i,j) (east endpoint, velocity vE); the edge velocity is the average of the two corner velocities times the edge length HTN(i,j), exactly the Fortran's edge-area reconstruction edgearea_n(i,j) = (vvel(i,j) + vvel(i-1,j))*p5*HTN(i,j)*dt (ice_transport_remap.F90:662-666), and cS/cN are the tracer values in the two cells sharing the edge (cell (i,j) and cell (i,j+1)), averaged to the face. The rule transport_flux_divergence binds the six values from the surrounding cells and U points and differences the four edge fluxes around the cell; the scheme caveat of transport_flux_e (incremental remap vs centered flux divergence, mass update at F90:3586-3590) applies identically. Pure combination algebra: no faq, no index sets of its own.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:stencil", "family:cice_bgrid", "grid:cice_bgrid", "op:advection"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), the horizontal transport edge reconstruction."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "transport_flux_n": {
      "params": ["cS", "cN", "vW", "vE", "HTN"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          "HTN",
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "+", "args": ["vW", "vE"] }, 2] },
              { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "+", "args": ["cS", "cN"] }, 2] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
